{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>To YHWH.</b> That he mentioned the Name, and the vow — if it be thus: I will give to HaShem such and such, or I will afflict myself." "<b>To swear.</b> A verb, and it comes with a name. And there are many like it." "<b>He shall not break his word.</b> Like לא יחלל (he shall not profane), and it is not the language of forgiveness. And we require received tradition, for the verse said 'a man and a woman' but did not specify when he is a man or when she is a woman."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:49.548366547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}